\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Kernel-specific predictive performance of the GG-KM models in 50 paired repeated holdouts of the melanoma cohort. Panel A shows the split-level IPCW integrated Brier score and Panel B the cure-discrimination area under the curve ($\mathrm  {AUC}_{\mathrm  {cure}}$) across the seven candidate kernels. Within each kernel, Poisson and negative-binomial GG-KM results are shown side by side, with color and hatching distinguishing the two latent-count laws. Each point represents one outer split, and the boxplots summarize the corresponding split-level distributions.}}{16}{figure.caption.11}\protected@file@percent }
